cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AgentGuard-IN in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "AgentGuard-IN: A Layered Defense Framework Against Indirect Prompt Injection on Tool-Using LLM Agents in Indian Digital Public Infrastructure"
authors:
  - name: "AgentGuard-IN Research Team"
year: 2026
url: "https://github.com/PrabhuVineeth/agentguard-in"
type: conference-paper
conference:
  name: "IEEE International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Cybersecurity"
keywords:
  - "large-language-models"
  - "ai-agents"
  - "prompt-injection"
  - "graph-neural-networks"
  - "digital-public-infrastructure"
  - "multilingual-safety"
  - "upi-security"
abstract: >-
  Autonomous tool-using LLM agents operating in Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI)
  are vulnerable to indirect prompt injection (IPI). AgentGuard-IN provides the
  first dedicated benchmark and layered defense combining multilingual subword
  screening, runtime trajectory graph anomaly detection (GraphSAGE), and an
  asymmetric three-tier triage policy (ALLOW / ESCALATE / BLOCK), cutting attack
  success from 61.6% to 2.4% with 0.0% false-block rate.
license: Apache-2.0

